File to edit: /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js

Current full contents:

```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```

Bug: `weekYear()` only handles the case where a late-December day belongs to week 1 of the NEXT year. It ignores the opposite direction: an early-January day whose `week()` is 52 or 53 belongs to the PREVIOUS week-year. This is observable in locales with `yearStart: 4` (e.g. `en-gb`, `fr`, `cs`), where e.g. `dayjs('2021-01-01').weekYear()` returns 2021 but should be 2020 (moment returns 2020).

Fix: add the missing January branch so the function becomes:

```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```

